============================================================
  global_alloc — comparative wall-clock tables (units per table; sized groups are ns/pair unless their header notes a composite/diagnostic unit)
============================================================

### Warm repeated bulk burst (`bench_direct_alloc` — alloc 1024 then free 1024 per iteration; NO reuse within one iteration's allocation half, but criterion reuses freed cache/freelist/pool blocks ACROSS iterations, so this is warm, not truly cold/first-touch; 1 alloc + 1 free per pair)

| Size | SeferAlloc (ns/pair) | mimalloc (ns/pair) | System (ns/pair) | Sefer vs mimalloc |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 16B | 20.0 | 6.0 | 71.5 | 3.34× slower |
| 64B | 21.2 | 9.7 | 75.2 | 2.17× slower |
| 256B | 21.3 | 11.9 | 69.3 | 1.79× slower |
| 1024B | 21.2 | 19.1 | 83.4 | 1.11× slower |

### Churn, non-writing (`bench_churn_alloc`, working-set reuse — 1 free + 1 alloc per pair)

| Size | SeferAlloc (ns/pair) | mimalloc (ns/pair) | System (ns/pair) | Sefer vs mimalloc |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 16B | 12.3 | 10.1 | 54.0 | 1.22× slower |
| 64B | 11.1 | 10.2 | 57.1 | 1.08× slower |
| 256B | 13.5 | 19.2 | 58.3 | **1.42× faster** |
| 1024B | 13.1 | 93.9 | 71.0 | **7.17× faster** |

### Churn + write (`bench_churn_alloc_write` — same as above, writes 16B after each alloc)

| Size | SeferAlloc (ns/pair) | mimalloc (ns/pair) | System (ns/pair) | Sefer vs mimalloc |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 16B | 11.7 | 9.6 | 52.4 | 1.22× slower |
| 64B | 12.1 | 11.6 | 57.1 | 1.04× slower |
| 256B | 14.2 | 16.7 | 64.3 | **1.18× faster** |
| 1024B | 16.0 | 97.0 | 70.8 | **6.06× faster** |

### Churn + teardown (`bench_global_alloc_churn_with_teardown`, DELIBERATE diagnostic — teardown stays inside timed region; the gap vs `global_alloc_churn` at the same size IS the segment decommit/release/re-reserve cost, see `benches/global_alloc.rs:658-667`)

| Size | SeferAlloc (ns/pair (composite, DIAGNOSTIC)) | mimalloc (ns/pair (composite, DIAGNOSTIC)) | System (ns/pair (composite, DIAGNOSTIC)) | Sefer vs mimalloc |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 16B | 15.0 | 10.2 | 58.3 | 1.47× slower |
| 64B | 19.7 | 11.9 | 66.1 | 1.66× slower |
| 256B | 16.8 | 13.2 | 79.4 | 1.27× slower |
| 1024B | 14.3 | 26.5 | 72.0 | **1.86× faster** |

